{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRuusrMaZNAsfbMshd6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Reasons for the move** (`adr/0009-split-workers-repo.md`, Context):\n- The workers team ships on a different cadence than the rest of the monorepo.\n- Their Python toolchain doubled the monorepo's CI time. The Consequences section says CI drops from 18 to 7 minutes after the move.\n\n**Effect of publishing shared types:** ADR 0004 (`adr/0004-monorepo.md`, Context) merged the repos partly because shared types drifted between the API and the web client twice in October 2023. ADR 0009 says the versioned `@acme/types` package, pinned by minor version, removes that drift problem, so the monorepo is no longer needed to prevent it. ADR 0009 supersedes ADR 0004. The cost is that a type change now needs a package release before workers can use it.\n\nI read the two ADRs directly and didn't run `graphify query` first, as the hook asked. I have no shell tool here to run the CLI."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1170,"cache_read_input_tokens":8959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1170},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d4ba66c-11ab-407d-bf66-acc277e1e58f","uuid":"5c0101d7-4fff-4ca4-9bec-0b513dd82807","timestamp":"2026-10-27T01:58:03.830Z","request_id":"req_011CgRuusdTb6mNMH4GTFCwB"}
